memcached is a high-performance, distributed memory object caching
system, generic in nature, but intended for use in speeding up dynamic
web applications by alleviating database load.

This extension uses libmemcached library to provide API for
communicating with memcached servers.

See also: https://github.com/php-memcached-dev/php-memcached

PECL memcached for php56 of azsupport/ports, built from ext/memcached
of the release tarball of azsupport/php-src, which bundles it:
lib/php/20131226/memcached.so, loaded by its ini in etc/php56/conf.d.
